module gunbc.rung_drop.let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup }
import gunbc.rung_drop { RungDrop, Standing, TypedDeclaration, Enumerated, ReplacementStaged }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }

// THE DECLARED RUNG DROP for the emitter's failure to annotate a let-bound closure's parameters with
// their declared formal types, so the emitted Rust does not compile without an expected-type context.
// Authored 2026-11-27 by fierce-lark-359 (planning slice) on warm-fox-517's ruling, approved as its
// own plan-only slice by neat-badger-614. No operator escalation was made for this row; no
// gunbc.design_ruling entry is claimed by this row and no operator words exist to record.
//
// WHAT THE DROP CARRIES. The repair of roadmap row emission-ownership-facts-survive-lowering requires
// the five arms of emission-building-block-realization to reach their declared output for the
// let-bound-closure subject family. Those five arms are acc_local_closure,
// acc_local_closure_identity_only, acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step,
// acc_local_closure_escaping_closure and acc_local_closure_copies_context. Each produces an instrument
// subject whose emitter output is a let-bound Rust closure, and the emitter writes those closures
// WITHOUT parameter type annotations, producing E0282 at compile time. This drop covers the emission
// half of those five arms: the emitter's obligation to annotate parameters from the subject's declared
// formal types at the binding site.
//
// WHAT THIS DROP DOES NOT COVER. It does not cover the fold-step lambda path, which emits WITH
// parameter types: v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_rust_fold_method_call calls
// v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_fold_lambda with acc_type_str and elem_type_str resolved from the
// fold's accumulator and element types, and v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_fold_lambda hands them to
// v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs as fallback_types with fold_acc_uses_fallback set, so
// every fold parameter renders with a declared type where inference yields none (positive control,
// re-measured 2026-11-27 on origin/main: 588 lines across 64 files under src/ carry a typed
// |acc: <RealType> annotation, including the emitter source itself and the tests that assert the
// emitted fold closures carry typed parameters, e.g. compiler_tests_rust asserting the emitted route
// contains "fold(walk_init(), |acc: Rc<Walk>, ...)"). It does not cover the instrument's semantic
// correctness, the subject's DAG declaration, or the claim execution. It does not cover
// v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs itself, which correctly prefers each parameter node's
// own RESOLVED type and falls back only when there is none; the failure is upstream of it --
// v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_let's ExprLambda arm passes elem_type_str: "_" to
// v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_collection_lambda, which wraps that "_" as the sole fallback_types
// entry it gives lambda_param_type_strs, so a let-bound parameter whose node resolves to nothing
// renders "_" through apply_type_template2 with spec.annotations.lambda_param_typed. It does not cover
// hand-written Rust in the emitted file (seed Rust is outside every worker's authority on this lane).
//
// WHY PREVIOUS IS MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE. The emitter's structural path mechanically resolves and
// writes formal parameter types where it is wired: emit_rust_fold_method_call derives lambda_acc_type_str
// and fold_elem_type_str from the fold call's resolved types, passes them to emit_typed_fold_lambda, and
// lambda_param_type_strs writes each parameter through apply_type_template2 with a resolved type or a
// supplied fallback. Positive control: 588 typed |acc: <RealType> annotation sites on origin/main,
// executing, compiling, with no expected-type context needed at the emitted closure. The mechanism is
// present and mechanically prevents untyped parameters wherever it fires. The five let-bound subjects
// fall off that mechanical path: emit_typed_let's ExprLambda arm hardcodes elem_type_str: "_" instead of
// resolving from the subject's declared formal parameter types, so the mechanism the fold path executes
// is not wired to their binding site. The rung is the minimum across the class's in-scope paths: where
// the mechanism is wired it holds MechanicallyPreventable; where it is not (the let-binding path), the
// population sits below it.
//
// WHY TEMPORARY IS MITIGATABLE. For the five let-bound subjects, the emitter produces bad output
// unconditionally: the parameter annotation is always "_", never a declared type. No mechanical check
// inside the emitter prevents this: emit_typed_let supplies the "_" fallback and lambda_param_type_strs
// renders it verbatim when the parameter node resolves to nothing. The E0282 at the emit-compile leg is
// a downstream consumer (rustc) catching bad emitter output, not the emitter preventing it. The emitter's
// own comment beside v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_fold_lambda records why the repair cannot be a
// one-word fallback change: "THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT THIS CHANGED THE FALLBACK TYPE STRING AND MEASURED NO
// EFFECT: lambda_param_type_strs prefers the parameter node's own RESOLVED type and only falls back when
// there is none ... The override has to sit where the parameter string is chosen, not where the fallback
// is supplied." So the fix is a wiring decision at the binding site, not a string swap, and until it is
// taken the worker's action is observation and reporting: name the hole at the leg where it fires and
// carry it, not attempt a fix in seed Rust (which is outside every worker's authority on this lane).
// This matches the precedent crate_row_names_a_module_the_emitter_has_no_reason_to_write: its 13 modules
// also never had the rung (no authored reference gave the emitter a reason to write their bodies), and
// the drop carries them at Mitigatable because the available action is reporting, not prevention.
//
// MEASURED BASIS, all counts re-printed on origin/main 2026-11-27, no slot spent. Untyped fallback
// census: the element-parameter shape "item: _|" appears 3 times under src/, all in the emitter's own
// seed source at src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs (two in v1_compiler_infer::realization_names,
// one in v1_compiler_infer::realization_declared_names) -- hand-written seed folds that leave the
// element parameter to inference, cited here as the same "_" fallback shape the let-bound path is forced
// into by emit_typed_let, not as emitted output. Typed census: the |acc: <RealType> shape appears on 588
// lines across 64 files under src/, spanning the emitter source, emitted seed folds, and the tests that
// assert the fold path's emitted annotations. The asymmetry is structural and sits in the plan, not in
// seed Rust: in src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag (module v1.compiler.emit_rust), emit_typed_let's ExprLambda arm
// passes elem_type_str: "_" to emit_typed_collection_lambda -- whose only use of it is
// fallback_types: [elem_type_str] into lambda_param_type_strs -- while emit_rust_fold_method_call
// derives lambda_acc_type_str and fold_elem_type_str from the fold call's resolved types and passes
// them to emit_typed_fold_lambda. Executed evidence of the consequence: tidy-hawk-691's acquisition on
// srv1 (slot 9, 2026-11-27T14:22:15Z, BOOT c095c0cd, head 435289c1c1129dbb3add4d4d12cc3063b20c84a0)
// emitted, for the accumulator-observation instrument, a let-bound closure without annotations --
// "let scale = |x: _| v1_rt::int_add(acc_int_identity(x.clone()), 1);" -- beside a fold-step lambda WITH
// them -- "fold(0, |acc: i64, x: i64| v1_rt::int_add(acc, scale(x.clone())))" -- and rustc answered with
// 3 error[E0282] among 5 errors total, first at subjects.rs:138:60, the acc_local_closure scale binding.
data let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types: RungDrop = RungDrop {
  identity: "let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types" as NonEmptyStr,

  subject: "the emitter's obligation to annotate a let-bound closure's parameters from the subject's declared formal types at the binding site, carried for the repair of emission-ownership-facts-survive-lowering and the five let-bound-closure arms of emission-building-block-realization: acc_local_closure, acc_local_closure_identity_only, acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step, acc_local_closure_escaping_closure and acc_local_closure_copies_context",

  declared: "2026-11-27",

  standing: Standing { declaration: TypedDeclaration {
    previous: MechanicallyPreventable,
    temporary: Mitigatable,
    reason: ReplacementStaged { replacement: "the emitter resolves each let-bound closure's declared formal parameter types at the binding site -- v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_let's ExprLambda arm, in place of passing elem_type_str: \"_\" to v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_collection_lambda -- and supplies them where v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs chooses each parameter string, so the emitted Rust compiles with no expected-type context" },
    population: Enumerated { members: FreeSemigroup { head: "acc_local_closure", tail: ["acc_local_closure_identity_only", "acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step", "acc_local_closure_escaping_closure", "acc_local_closure_copies_context"] } },
    restoration_trigger: "THE EMITTER ANNOTATES A LET-BOUND CLOSURE'S PARAMETERS FROM THE SUBJECT'S DECLARED FORMAL TYPES AT THE BINDING SITE, so the emitted Rust compiles with no expected-type context. Specifically: v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_let resolves each parameter's declared formal type at its ExprLambda arm and threads it through v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_collection_lambda into v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs at the point where the parameter string is chosen -- per that function's own documented note, changing only the fallback string measures no effect -- replacing the elem_type_str: \"_\" that arm passes today. Two things do NOT retire this drop: (1) rerunning the same instrument unchanged, which reproduces the same E0282 at the emit-compile leg; and (2) hand-writing Rust parameter annotations in the emitted file, which is seed Rust and is outside every worker's authority on this lane. A default or timed-out closure of any ask is not a ruling. No operator words exist for this row; none were sought.",
  } }
}
